Because we don't really know if it gets read somewhere.

Example:

``` js
let foo;

function bar() {
    foo = 'hello world';
    console.log(foo);
};

function baz() {
    console.info(window.foo);
}
```

This example is reported as a problem:

```
1:5  error  'foo' is never modified, use 'const' instead  prefer-const
```
